# Account.Search keeps the newest matches: of uids 3, 7 and 9 with a limit
# of 2 it fetches 7 and 9. Hand-written (see login_list.imap)
S: * OK [CAPABILITY IMAP4rev1 AUTH=PLAIN] IMAP4 service ready
C: a1 LOGIN "someone@example.com" "app-pass"
S: a1 OK user logged in
C: a2 EXAMINE "INBOX"
S: * 3 EXISTS
S: a2 OK [READ-ONLY] EXAMINE completed
C: a3 UID SEARCH ALL
S: * SEARCH 3 7 9
S: a3 OK SEARCH completed
C: a4 UID FETCH 7,9 (UID FLAGS RFC822.SIZE INTERNALDATE BODY.PEEK[HEADER.FIELDS (DATE FROM TO CC SUBJECT MESSAGE-ID IN-REPLY-TO REFERENCES)])
S: * 2 FETCH (UID 7 FLAGS () RFC822.SIZE 100 INTERNALDATE " 3-Nov-2026 09:15:00 -0600" BODY[HEADER.FIELDS (DATE FROM TO CC SUBJECT MESSAGE-ID IN-REPLY-TO REFERENCES)] {#}
L: Subject: older
L:
S: )
S: * 3 FETCH (UID 9 FLAGS (\Seen) RFC822.SIZE 100 INTERNALDATE " 4-Nov-2026 09:15:00 -0600" BODY[HEADER.FIELDS (DATE FROM TO CC SUBJECT MESSAGE-ID IN-REPLY-TO REFERENCES)] {#}
L: Subject: newer
L:
S: )
S: a4 OK FETCH completed
C: a5 LOGOUT
S: * BYE logging out
S: a5 OK LOGOUT completed
